# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_17045> (dinitrogen oxide)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_17045> "A nitrogen oxide consisting of linear unsymmetrical molecules with formula N<small><sub>2</sub></small>O. While it is the most used gaseous anaesthetic in the world, its major commercial use, due to its solubility under pressure in vegetable fats combined with its non-toxicity in low concentrations, is as an aerosol spray propellant and aerating agent for canisters of 'whipped' cream.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "KEGG_COMPOUND") <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_17045> "Dinitrogen oxide")
