# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_44658> (okadaic acid)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_44658> "A polycyclic ether that is produced by several species of dinoflagellates, and is known to accumulate in both marine sponges and shellfish.  A polyketide, polyether derivative of a C<small><sub>38</sub></small> fatty acid, it is one of the primary causes of diarrhetic shellfish poisoning (DSP). It is a potent inhibitor of specific protein phosphatases and is known to have a variety of negative effects on cells.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_44658> "CHEBI:44658")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_44658> "okadaic acid")
