# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_8674> (pyrimethanil)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_8674> "A member of the class of aminopyrimidines that is <em>N</em>-phenylpyrimidin-2-amine carrying two additional methyl substituents at positions 4 and 6.  A fungicide used to control grey mould on fruit, vegetables and ornamentals as well as leaf scab on pome fruit. Also commonly employed to control <em>Botrytis cinerea</em> throughout the winemaking process in grapes, must, fermenting must and wine.")
