# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00001151> (citrus fruit food product)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00001151> "A citrus fruit is botanically classified as a type of berry called a hesperidium that has a thick, leathery rind, with numerous oil glands, and a large flesh portion composed of several wedge-shaped sections. Unlike pome fruit, such as the apple, the citrus fruit is derived from a superior ovary, an ovary completely separate from the calyx."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00001151> "citrus fruit food product"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00001151> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00001057>)

