AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00001564> "Blood meal is a dry, inert powder made from blood used as a high-nitrogen organic fertilizer and a high protein animal feed."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00001564> <https://bioregistry.io/reference/siren:F10831>)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00001564> "It is one of the highest non-synthetic sources of nitrogen. It usually comes from cattle or hogs as a slaughterhouse by-product. N = 13.25%, P = 1.0%, K = 0.6%.

SIREN DB annotation:
* medium ground FOODON:03430117
* blood UBERON:0000178
* water removal process FOODON:03460138
* preservation by dehydration or drying FOODON:03470116
* animal as consumer FOODON:03510021"@en)
