AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411222> "A gill-bearing aquatic craniate animal that lacks limbs with digits."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411222> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B1222>)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411222> "\"Most fish are ectothermic ('cold-blooded'), allowing their body temperatures to vary as ambient temperatures change, though some of the large active swimmers like white shark and tuna can hold a higher core temperature.\" - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fish"@en)
